  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Garrafina. Play on your own train from the opening double; after a player passes their train is open until its end changes. Passing is only legal when no playable tile exists. Score by opponents' remaining pips or blocked-hand pip differences.",
    Player: 'Garrafina: extend your train when possible, exploit open opponent trains, and avoid passing into vulnerability.',
    objective: 'Play all tiles first, or in a blocked hand have the lowest pip total on unplayed tiles.',
    gameplay: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
    keyRules: [
      'If a legal tile exists on any currently legal train, passing is not allowed.',
      'Open-train status is tied to pass state and can close again when its end changes.',
      'In blocked hands, lowest pip total wins; if two or more tie for least spots, there is no winner and no one scores.',
      'Session end is by agreed deal count or agreed target score.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 4 players; four-player is the base form.',
      deck: 'One double-six domino set of 28 tiles.',
      equipment: 'Optional train markers to show which trains are open after a pass.',
      dealing: 'Deal 7 tiles to each player. In 4-player games all tiles are dealt. In 3-player games one 7-tile heap remains face down. In 2-player games two 7-tile heaps remain face down.',
    },
    turnFlow: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
